<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss newspaper ad pages fall 7.4 pct in May y/y.</title>
<headline>Swiss newspaper ad pages fall 7.4 pct in May y/y.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advertising pages in Swiss newspapers fell 7.4 percent in May compared with a year earlier after a 3.3 percent rise in April, according to figures compiled by the WEMF media tracking agency.</p>
<p> (pct change in pages vs year-ago)	May	Jan-May</p>
<p> Daily/weekly newspapers		  - 7.4	- 7.1</p>
<p> Commercial ads			     - 6.7	- 5.0</p>
<p>    Employment ads			 - 13.6     - 22.1</p>
<p> Free newspapers			    - 8.6	- 3.6</p>
<p>    Commercial ads			  - 7.2	- 1.3</p>
<p>    Employment ads			 - 27.8     - 31.9</p>
<p> Magazines				    - 8.4	- 4.3</p>
<p>    Multicolour ads			 - 0.9	+ 0.1</p>
<p>    Black and white ads		  - 29.7     - 15.7</p>
<p> Specialised publications		- 13.4	- 8.7</p>
<p>    Multicolour ads			 - 3.3	+ 4.7</p>
<p>    Black and white ads		  - 18.7     - 14.4</p>
<p>The Association of Swiss Advertising Companies (VSW) said the figures reflected in part a drop of 116 overall print-media editions in May compared with the same month of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
